Transparency about product sourcing, manufacturing, materials, and impact builds consumer trust while enabling informed decisions about reuse and circular participation. Open disclosure of environmental and social information differentiates responsible products and justifies price premiums for sustainable alternatives. Transparency also facilitates informed decision-making by consumers and reverse logistics partners about product condition, repairability, and material composition. Design for transparency includes accessible documentation, labeling systems, and digital tools that communicate product history and composition without overwhelming users.